{#-
  VideoEmbed (SPEC §9.1, §15.1; HANDOFF §5, §7): the click-to-load facade.
  Only partials/video-block.njk calls it: every video on the site is the
  one video template (SPEC §7.5), so no page sets up a facade of its own.
  The YouTube note is once per page, at its end (notices/video.njk).

    {% from "partials/video.njk" import videoEmbed %}
    {{ videoEmbed(video, bleed='page') }}

  Arguments:
    video   a video from `videoById` (or `introChapters`/`solutionsByTier`)
    bleed   'inset' (default): rounded frame inside the column.
            'page': below 600px the frame runs to the screen edges
            (cancels the page gutter). 'card': below 600px it runs to the
            card's edges (cancels the card's padding), with square corners.

  Every facade is the same (project lead, 2026-11-09): the 72px play disc
  (56px below 600px), the duration badge, and the settling arc at the
  frame's base from 600px when the video has no thumbnail. The title is
  the play control's accessible name and isn't repeated on the frame: the
  video template's heading names the video beside (or above) it.

  The facade names the page's YouTube note (id youtube-note-text, rendered
  by the page's layout) in aria-describedby, so the note is heard with the
  play control although it is at the end of the page (SPEC §9.1: pressing
  play is an informed choice).

  Without JavaScript the facade is a "Watch on YouTube" link. src/js/players.js
  turns it into a "Play video" button that loads the YouTube player only when
  pressed: nothing here contacts YouTube (no iframe, API script, preconnect or
  YouTube thumbnail). The frame shows the video's self-hosted thumbnail
  (media/thumbs/) if it has one, otherwise the plain night-teal frame.

  A placeholder video (a blank youtube_url in data/videos.csv) shows
  "[Video coming soon]" and has no link or button. The page's note is still
  shown, so the page reads as it will at launch.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- macro videoEmbed(video, bleed='inset') -%}
{%- set spoken = video.duration | spokenDuration -%}
<div class="video video--{{ bleed }}{% if video.placeholder %} video--placeholder{% endif %}" data-video="{{ video.video_id }}"{% if not video.placeholder %} data-youtube-id="{{ video.youtube_id }}"{% endif %} data-title="{{ video.title }}">
  <div class="video__frame">
    <div class="video__media">
      {%- if video.thumbnail %}<img class="video__thumb" src="/media/thumbs/{{ video.thumbnail }}" alt="" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      {%- else %}{#- The boards' flatter video arc (Problem-A, Intro-B), not the hero's (partials/arc.njk). -#}
      <svg class="arc arc--video" viewBox="0 0 960 120" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M0 120 L0 80 Q480 10 960 80 L960 120 Z"/></svg>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {%- if video.placeholder %}
    <div class="video__facade video__facade--placeholder">
      <span class="video__title visually-hidden">{{ video.title }}</span>
      <span class="video__soon">[Video coming soon]</span>
      <span class="duration-badge video__duration">{{ video.duration }}</span>
    </div>
    {%- else %}
    <a class="video__facade" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v={{ video.youtube_id }}" rel="noreferrer" aria-describedby="youtube-note-text">
      <span class="video__action visually-hidden">Watch on YouTube: </span>
      <span class="video__title visually-hidden">{{ video.title }}</span>
      <span class="play-disc" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon('play', 28, 'play-disc__icon') }}</span>
      <span class="duration-badge video__duration" aria-hidden="true">{{ video.duration }}</span>
      {%- if spoken %}<span class="visually-hidden">, {{ spoken }}</span>{% endif %}
    </a>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
